  introductionDescription: A strong steel cable for suspending a bridge deck.
    Connect it to secure anchors so it can support the deck in tension.
  introductionImage: {fileID: 0}
  almanacDescription: A taut steel cable carries tension and transfers load from the
    deck to towers or anchorages. A slack cable stops supporting the deck, and it
    cannot carry compression. Use rigid towers or braces for members that must resist
    pushing forces. Each placement adds a matching cable on either side of the bridge.
